<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver rise on world prices.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver rise on world prices.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold and silver prices rose on Tuesday at the local market helped by overnight gains in world prices and seasonal domestic demand, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) settled 200 rupees higher at 56,600 per piece after losing 300 rupees on Monday and 1,000 rupees last week.</p>
<p>Traders said supplies of smuggled gold was restricted due to tighter vigil by the customs authorities and this pushed prices higher in moderate trade.  </p>
